        {
            "name": "Ben-Tsiyon Alfes",
            "bio": "Ben-Tsiyon (also Ben-Zion) Alfes (Hebrew: בן-ציון אלפס‎) (1851-1941) was a rabbi, author, prolific author of Yiddish religious literature, commentator and compiler of prayers in vernacular Yiddish. His most well-known book is <em>Maaseh Alfes</em> (Tales of Alfes). The last work he saw published, written at age 90, was an autobiography titled \"The Life Story of the Maase Alfes.\" Another work, <em>Toledot ve-Zikhronot</em>, also an autobiography, but with a different focus, was published posthumously.",
            "website": "http://yleksikon.blogspot.com/2014/07/ben-tsion-benzion-alfes.html",
